# The memory map, checked from inside the machine.
#
# data/memory-map.json is extracted from BIOS.cfg and BIOS.inc (GREP); this
# case is the other half of that claim (INSPECT/RUN), so a linker-config change
# that moves a boundary turns the docs red instead of quietly wrong.
#
#   861/862  BAS_TXTTAB ($035D) must hold $0800  — where programs start
#   871/872  BAS_MEMSIZ ($0367) must hold $8000  — top of usable RAM
#   40960    $A000  first byte of the Kernal jump table: JMP abs ($4C)
#   41176    $A0D8  first reserved slot: also a JMP, to the RTS stub
#   41120/1  $A09F  NvStat's JMP target must differ from the reserved slot's,
#   41177/8  $A0D9  or the ROM under test is older than v1.6
#   41137    $A0B1  VdpInfo, the first PICOVDP entry: JMP abs
#   41138/9  $A0B2  its target must differ from the reserved slot's, or the
#                   ROM under test is older than v2.0
#   65280    $FF00  Wozmon: LDA #$1B ($A9)

expect ^PASS$
absent ^FAIL
